WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:03.148
- You make that choice,
either you can go this way

00:00:03.148 --> 00:00:06.508
where it's all bad and
cloudy and feel like a victim

00:00:06.508 --> 00:00:08.857
or you could feel like
you've conquered everything

00:00:08.857 --> 00:00:11.566
that they told you that you couldn't do

00:00:11.566 --> 00:00:13.234
and be out here winning, so it's like,

00:00:13.234 --> 00:00:14.817
psh, let me go over here and win.

00:00:14.817 --> 00:00:17.650
(uplifting music)

00:00:19.361 --> 00:00:22.530
I started realizing that
something was off with my body

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:25.113
when I was around 14 years old.

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:29.701
After awhile, my mom was in
her room and she called me

00:00:29.701 --> 00:00:32.431
to the back and she
was like, you have ALS.

00:00:32.431 --> 00:00:34.614
And I was like, okay.

00:00:34.614 --> 00:00:37.510
And she was like, do
you know what that is?

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:39.093
And I was like, no.

00:00:44.571 --> 00:00:48.074
The role my family and
friends play into my life

00:00:48.074 --> 00:00:50.223
is so significant.

00:00:50.223 --> 00:00:51.760
My mom flew down.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:54.986
They didn't start babying
me, they didn't tell me

00:00:54.986 --> 00:00:58.141
anything negative, anything
that I said I wanted to do,

00:00:58.141 --> 00:01:00.566
they supported it, it was
senior year in high school

00:01:00.566 --> 00:01:03.499
and we went to grad night
Disneyland and because

00:01:03.499 --> 00:01:06.850
Disneyland was so big, the
school nurse recommended

00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:10.215
that I use a motorized wheelchair

00:01:10.215 --> 00:01:12.894
and it was so convenient
for me, I was like,

00:01:12.894 --> 00:01:15.844
well college is almost
as big as Disneyland,

00:01:15.844 --> 00:01:17.834
I might as well start using a chair.

00:01:17.834 --> 00:01:19.996
And that's the thing, is like
I know people will probably

00:01:19.996 --> 00:01:23.367
see me in my wheelchair and
think, oh it's a wheelchair,

00:01:23.367 --> 00:01:26.066
it's the worst thing that
could ever happen to somebody

00:01:26.066 --> 00:01:30.372
but in my case and I do
have to put the disclaimer

00:01:30.372 --> 00:01:33.257
that every person with a
disability is different,

00:01:33.257 --> 00:01:35.177
if I would have kept walking,
I probably would have been

00:01:35.177 --> 00:01:36.815
more permanent in the chair.

00:01:36.815 --> 00:01:39.288
One of the major reasons why
I even started my YouTube

00:01:39.288 --> 00:01:43.449
was because I wanted
to show that disability

00:01:43.449 --> 00:01:46.717
didn't look sad, it didn't look sloppy,

00:01:46.717 --> 00:01:50.330
it didn't look medical, it
could be fly, it could be sexy,

00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:54.140
it could be fun, it could be
whatever you wanted it to be.

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:57.891
Because it's so annoying as
a person with a disability

00:01:57.891 --> 00:02:01.685
when people think that you
should look a certain way.

00:02:01.685 --> 00:02:04.838
There's been so many times
where people will come up to me

00:02:04.838 --> 00:02:06.694
if I'm not in my chair and be like,

00:02:06.694 --> 00:02:08.014
well you don't look disabled.

00:02:08.014 --> 00:02:09.669
What the fuck is that supposed to mean?

00:02:09.669 --> 00:02:12.259
Oh so you think I'm
supposed to be here like,

00:02:12.259 --> 00:02:16.334
oh I'm sad, my life is the
worst, and it's just like no,

00:02:16.334 --> 00:02:17.834
sorry, I sit high.

00:02:19.295 --> 00:02:21.637
So the average life
expectancy for a person

00:02:21.637 --> 00:02:26.112
who was diagnosed with ALS
is about five to seven years

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:29.029
and given the fact that I'll be 30.

00:02:30.181 --> 00:02:33.385
I've doubled the life
expectancy and then some.

00:02:33.385 --> 00:02:37.186
I used to have a fear
that because I was a woman

00:02:37.186 --> 00:02:40.346
in a wheelchair, that I
wouldn't be able to do as much

00:02:40.346 --> 00:02:43.089
as I wanted but I always
have to get back centered

00:02:43.089 --> 00:02:47.521
and just remember, in this
moment, you can either

00:02:47.521 --> 00:02:50.283
harp on all the things
that haven't happened yet,

00:02:50.283 --> 00:02:53.730
all the fears which is just a
thought, it's not even real,

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:56.845
or you can look at what is real.

00:02:56.845 --> 00:02:58.652
You still have the ability to walk,

00:02:58.652 --> 00:03:00.700
you still have the ability to stand,

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:03.590
you still have the ability
to speak and open your eyes

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:06.356
and with that alone,
it's like, you know what,

00:03:06.356 --> 00:03:10.567
I'm going this way and
remind myself that I'm always

00:03:10.567 --> 00:03:14.151
going to push through, I'm
always gonna stay positive

00:03:14.151 --> 00:03:16.446
and I'm going to do the best that I can

00:03:16.446 --> 00:03:20.630
to be the best version of
me, 'cause I sit high boo.

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:23.213
(upbeat music)

